From 5ff400ee9a6c1ec36c3c4aa031a6eb1902b0ccf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Cl=C3=A9ment=20Le=20Goffic?= <legoffic.clement@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:53:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] arm64: renesas: defconfig: Disable the SCMI power domain
 provider
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Once the scmi_devpd provider probes successfully, the Linux power
domain housekeeping sends POWER_STATE_SET(OFF) to unclaimed domains
and takes the CMN interconnect domain down, which kills the AP.
The device tree power-domain ids do not match the SCP domain table
yet, so no working domain control is lost by turning it off.
Disable the provider until the id contract and the SCP side agent
permissions are in place.

Co-developed-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Clément Le Goffic <clegoffic@baylibre.com>
---
 arch/arm64/configs/renesas_defconfig | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/configs/renesas_defconfig b/arch/arm64/configs/renesas_defconfig
index fc8a71d08cc1..be7f31119671 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/configs/renesas_defconfig
+++ b/arch/arm64/configs/renesas_defconfig
@@ -122,6 +122,7 @@ CONFIG_PCI_PWRCTRL_SLOT=y
 CONFIG_DEVTMPFS=y
 CONFIG_DEVTMPFS_MOUNT=y
 CONFIG_ARM_SCMI_PROTOCOL=y
+# CONFIG_ARM_SCMI_POWER_DOMAIN is not set
 CONFIG_ARM_SCMI_POWER_CONTROL=y
 # CONFIG_DMIID is not set
 CONFIG_MTD=y
-- 
